     Kafka was rejected primarily due to the significant operational complexity and the steep learning curve for a team with no prior experience, given the tight 2-week setup/migration constraint and modest budget. While Kafka excels in high-throughput,[0m[2m highly durable, and truly distributed stream processing with robust native support for exactly-once semantics, introducing it would likely:
